WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:02.125
Picture the inquiry tracker from Lesson 1.

00:00:02.508 --> 00:00:05.956
Its owner says: "Requests are in too many places, I forget

00:00:05.991 --> 00:00:09.938
to respond, and I need help." That sentence is valuable,

00:00:10.263 --> 00:00:12.562
but it contains several possible products.

00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:16.277
We could build a shared inbox, a spreadsheet, an automated

00:00:16.324 --> 00:00:18.866
email service, or an inquiry dashboard.

00:00:19.377 --> 00:00:22.256
Your first job is to express the real problem in your own

00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:22.860
language.

00:00:23.185 --> 00:00:27.167
Include frustration, examples, constraints, and things you

00:00:27.237 --> 00:00:28.224
have not decided.

00:00:28.607 --> 00:00:30.987
You do not need to sort it into the perfect order.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:34.040
Ask the agent to hold its response until you say you are

00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:34.528
finished.
